Darn.  It is better, if you can manage it, to level your pets up 
faster than you.  When you get experience, you level up.  When the 
kittens get experience, they grow, first into housecats, and then 
into large cats.  As a level-6 character, you should have at least
housecats by now.  By the time you reach minetown, they are likely 
to be killed unless they have by that time become large cats.

Your strength is used to help determine how tough the monsters that 
get generated are.  And at level 6, you're so strong (level 6) that 
the game will often generate monsters your kittens can't successfully 
fight.  The good news is that if your kittens don't attack something, 
it won't attack them.  The bad news is that if you fight them because 
your pets don't, you'll continue to level up faster than your pets, 
and they'll become first useless and eventually dead. 

So, be careful.  Up until minetown, whenever your kitties engage 
something in combat, it means that it's something they can probably 
handle.  Softening it up for them is okay, but be sure to let them 
kill it if at all possible.  Don't kill it yourself! And I know 
this seems perverse, but try to minimize leveling up yourself until 
your pets are more dangerous than you. 

